WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.837
Let's start off by talking about
belongings in your daily life.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.680
Do you prefer having fewer or more
belongings in your daily life?

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.520
I think, personally, for me,
I'd prefer having fewer belongings just

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.360
because I feel like it would be more
easier to deal with on a daily basis,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.757
especially when it comes to technology,
trying to decide if I had a laptop

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.677
and an iPad and a phone,
I have all three of the same kind of thing.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.000
I just think it would be easier
to function in life with less.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.760
What things can you not live without?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.077
My phone.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.280
I can't live without my phone.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.440
What else can't I live without?

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.800
Water, always staying hydrated,
and my cats.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.040
How do you organize your belongings?

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.960
Sometimes I do it by color.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:02.400
If it was things related to books, I like
to organize them by colors on the shelves, yeah.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.040
Now, let's talk about
technology in modern life.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.560
How has technology changed your life?

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.840
I think technology has changed
my life in so many different ways,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.597
one of them being the ability
to connect with people.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.917
Personally, I have a lot of long distance
friends,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.640
and technology has allowed me to stay
in touch with those people,

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.157
and even though they're not with you
personally, you do feel like you never

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.440
miss that connection
because of technology.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.320
I think work-related technology offers

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.800
me a lot of opportunity to connect

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.880
and network with many different kind of people.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.320
Would you like to have more technology in
your life or less technology in your life?

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:00.570
I personally would like to have less
technology in my life just because I feel like

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.800
technology sometimes defeats

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.400
the purpose of humanity in a sense of

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.157
if there's too much of it,
like nowadays with the AI and all of that,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.557
it's kind of starting to replace
human beings in a sense.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.400
I would like to depend less
on technology, generally.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.600
Do you think technology has made your life
better now than in the past

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.277
when you had less technology?

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:33.600
Yes, to a certain extent,
just because I feel like back then,

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.637
we didn't have Instagram,
we didn't have those, the iconic social media

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.760
platforms that all young teenagers use.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.397
And those are the main platforms people
are using now to connect with people

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.360
and to network, and especially if
you're running your own business.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.840
For example, trying to share your music or
share art, that's how you

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.800
come out to a bigger platform.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.120
So definitely, I feel like it
has a bigger advantage

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.120
than what we had in the past.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.000
Now, let's talk about reading.

00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:08.440
Do you enjoy reading?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.597
I do enjoy reading,
but I wish I did more of it.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:19.437
I feel like with technology and all
the modern things coming up,

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:24.797
I feel like I used to read more as a
child, and I'm trying to get back into it.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.400
Some of the things I love
reading about are self-help books.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.820
Those are my favorite.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.840
Now, let's talk about outdoor activities.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.557
What activities do you
like to do outdoors?

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.240
Outdoors, I love to go running sometimes.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.360
I like to do morning yogas.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.240
I've had yogas by the beach before.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:50.640
I really love joining group
classes outdoors as well.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.517
I once did this thing
where we started off with a morning yoga,

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.960
and then it went into a HIIT workout,
and then a yoga cool down.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.277
I love to go swimming.
I love the ocean.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.040
I love to be by the beach.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.280
How often do you spend time outside?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:14.957
Not as often as I would like, just because
given the location I'm in right now,

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:19.040
It gets pretty hot and humid,
and I wish our weather would

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.320
accommodate being outdoors more often.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.520
But I try my best to be
outside as much as possible.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.560
When you are outside, do you prefer
being alone or with other people?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.920
I think I prefer being alone just because
it

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.597
gives you that space to be with yourself
and to disconnect

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.200
from everyone around you.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.160
For me, personally, sometimes I feel like
when I'm around people,

00:04:45.243 --> 00:04:47.997
my social battery dies very quickly,

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.317
and it could be a lot to take in.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.877
Both have their advantages
and disadvantages.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.812
Of course, I'd love to hang out
with my friends and be around my friends but,

00:05:00.012 --> 00:05:04.600
I recently did a solo trip to England,
and I spent most of my time by myself

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.840
in nature, walking around the city.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.920
I find that one learns a lot when they
spend time with their self and

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.520
the energies around them.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.880
In the future, would you like
to do more activities outdoors?

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.357
Yes, for sure.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.037
I always wanted to try
out paragliding, skiing.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.840
Skiing has been one of like, an outdoor
activity I'd always wanted to do.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:35.677
A time where I had to adapt to a new situation,
it came when I graduated from high school

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.680
and I had to finally move to college.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:43.840
And I was one of the people that decided
ultimately to move out of my home place

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.920
to go abroad for university
just because I felt like university abroad

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.040
had more resources and opportunity.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.800
It was pretty difficult to fit in.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:03.880
People have different culture over there,
different outlook on life,

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.837
but I needed to adapt because that was the

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:12.800
only way I could grow in that environment.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.080
I think that some days were
better than others.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:22.117
It was pretty difficult in the beginning
just because I felt like...

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:26.200
In the beginning,
you feel very out of place.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:31.080
For example, when I started my degree,
I didn't really had prior experience

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:35.880
to the art world and everything related
to the art world in my home country.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:42.440
So when I moved, I kind of was that one student
in between everyone that was

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.040
inexperienced or less experienced,

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.797
and it got to me sometimes.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.717
Sometimes I cried in class.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.080
I had my breakdowns.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:55.637
But I think I learned a lot that you keep
pushing through in those situations.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:07:00.837
It could be so easy to cave
in to the bad or the negative.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:05.160
But if you just take
it as a learning experience and

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:09.680
keep moving,
after a year, two years pass by,

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.237
one starts to acclimate to their
environment and one

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.760
starts to adapt properly.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.797
We have been talking about a new
situation you had to adapt to.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.477
We're going to continue to talk about
change and adaptation and personal

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:24.680
growth, things like that.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:29.240
Why do some people find it harder
to adapt to change than others?

