00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:01.797
I think as human beings,
we, we don't like change.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.320
I think humans like to stay the same.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.317
We grow up, our brain.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:12.717
Our brain, the way it's formulated, is
that we get specific programs

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.160
put into us when we're kids.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.240
And straying away from those kind of programs,
whether it's

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.637
the environment you grew up in or
the relationships you've had throughout

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:29.640
your life, I think it puts the human
being in a state of fight or flight.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:34.240
That's why some people resist
change or never want to change.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.760
Now, let's talk about cultural adaptation.

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:41.200
Why do some people adapt more
easily to living abroad than others?

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:46.597
I think sometimes a person
finds themselves abroad.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:52.880
Maybe that culture fits them
more as a person, as a soul.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.760
I think that sometimes people find,

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.757
they empathize with the people

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.237
that they live with outside.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:08.277
And if one is reserved in their home
country and decides to move out, they open

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.480
themselves up to different experiences.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.637
And I think
when one finds that freedom

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:20.360
and that belonging somewhere else,
they start to adapt a new

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.520
lifestyle and way of living.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.080
What challenges do people face
when adapting to a new culture?

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:32.400
One of the many challenges I think people
face when adapting to a new culture is

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.917
sometimes there are some things about
that culture that will not

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.960
resonate with you as a person.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.877
For example, me personally,
I decided to ultimately move out

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:49.837
of America after I got my degree just
because there were a couple of values

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.720
in that culture that personally
I didn't resonate with.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:59.240
And I found it better to find elsewhere,
somewhere elsewhere, where I

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:06.280
I could feel more at home and more like
everything was in coherence with me.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:10.640
And last question in part three,
how does facing challenges help

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.280
people develop as individuals?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:17.320
I think facing challenges,
most importantly,

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:22.600
makes you listen to yourself more,
makes you follow your gut more.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:29.677
And I'm a personal believer that
nobody grows without pain

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.760
and going through challenges.

00:10:30.843 --> 00:10:35.240
I think pain is a big life teacher.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:40.997
It's something that people have
to go through in order to become

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.840
a better version of themselves.

